<title>USA: Astra USA buys periodontal therapy rights.</title>
<headline>Astra USA buys periodontal therapy rights.</headline>
<dateline>WESTBOROUGH, Mass. 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Astra USA, a unit of Swedish pharmaceutical company Astra AB, said it acquired U.S. licensing rights to PerioChip from Perio Products Ltd, a unit of Israel Chemicals Ltd.</p>
<p>PerioChip is a biodegradable polymer, containing chlorohexidine gluconate, an agent used to kill bacteria which cause periodontal disease, it said.</p>
<p>Perio Products, which develops new periodontal technology, recently filed a new drug application with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for PerioChip, Astra USA said.</p>
<p>The polymer was being investigated in the United States as an adjunctive therapy with root planing, the company said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
